WEBVTT

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.761
Here's a song I downloaded.

00:00:05.811 --> 00:00:07.482
Mariah Carey, Bye Bye.

00:00:07.532 --> 00:00:10.063
And look at the file in Explorer.

00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:12.487
No cover art. Just a plain icon.

00:00:12.537 --> 00:00:13.710
Let's fix that.

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:20.829
I'll open Audio Album Art Embedder, and
choose the folder with my music.

00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:25.755
It finds the song, and it spots the cover
image on its own.

00:00:25.805 --> 00:00:27.031
There's the preview.

00:00:27.081 --> 00:00:30.843
If it picked the wrong one, I can choose a
different image.

00:00:32.048 --> 00:00:35.208
Everything's ticked, so I just click,
Embed cover art.

00:00:35.712 --> 00:00:38.377
And that's it. One of one file updated.

00:00:38.427 --> 00:00:44.142
Just keep in mind, the file is changed in
place, so keep a backup if it matters.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.678
Back in Explorer, it's the same file, and
now the cover shows up as its thumbnail.

00:00:52.728 --> 00:00:53.920
Before, and after.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:01.006
It works with MP3, FLAC, M4A and AAC
files.

00:01:01.056 --> 00:01:04.920
Try it on a copy of your own music folder.

